  "guid": "com.nadeko.sptmo2pluginv4",
  "name": "SPTarkov ModOrganizer 2 Plugin",
  "slug": "sptarkov-modorganizer-2-plugin",
  "teaser": "Adds Mod Organizer 2 support for SPT 4.x",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/WUHKtKAgGGYNu6SLmMLBJsVm7yLCXORqsP4AzjZ5.png",
  "downloads": 978,
  "favourites_count": 13,
  "description": "<p>Manage SPT 4.x mods with Mod Organizer 2. Inspired by <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/964/spt-modorganizer-integration\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SPT ModOrganizer Integration</a>.</p>\n<p>Please report any problems in the comments.</p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Adds a <strong>Launch SPT</strong> button that starts the SPT server, then opens the launcher when it is ready.</li>\n<li>Adds separate <strong>SPT Server</strong> and <strong>SPT Launcher</strong> entries for troubleshooting.</li>\n<li>Installs client mods to <code>BepInEx/plugins</code>.</li>\n<li>Installs server mods to <code>SPT/user/mods</code>.</li>\n<li>Keeps your profiles, logs, launcher data, certificates, and settings in your real SPT folder.</li>\n<li>Keeps server mods managed by MO2, so you can enable or disable them without manually moving files.</li>\n<li>Recognizes common SPT mod archive layouts during installation.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Requirements</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mod Organizer 2 2.5.x</li>\n<li>SPT 4.x</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Extract the plugin into your Mod Organizer 2 installation folder.</li>\n<li>Start MO2 and create or select an SPT instance.</li>\n<li>When MO2 asks for your game folder, select your SPT client root.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Choose the folder that contains:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>EscapeFromTarkov.exe</code></li>\n<li><code>BepInEx</code></li>\n<li><code>winhttp.dll</code></li>\n<li><code>SPT</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>For example, choose <code>C:\\Games\\SPT</code>, not <code>C:\\Games\\SPT\\SPT</code>.</p>\n",
  "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2799/sptarkov-modorganizer-2-plugin",
  "fika_compatibility": false,
  "featured": false,
  "contains_ads": false,
  "contains_ai_content": true,
  "custom_ai_disclosure": "<p>AI was used as a development assistant for automated testing, drafting documentation, checking wording, and helping review implementation details.</p>\n<p>The plugin code and release decisions were manually reviewed and tested against a real MO2/SPT Portable setup before publication.</p>\n",
